## Document Operations

### Methods

**Add content:**
- `append_text`: Add paragraph. Params: `text`, `bold?`, `italic?`
- `append_heading`: Add heading. Params: `text`, `level` (1-6)
- `append_list`: Add list. Params: `items` (array), `ordered?`

**Replace content at position:**
- `update_text`: Replace block. Params: `position`, `text`, `bold?`, `italic?`
- `update_heading`: Replace with heading. Params: `position`, `text`, `level`

**Core:**
- `create`: New document. Params: `table_id`, `field_id`, `title`, `row_id?`
- `list`: List all documents
- `read`: Get content. Params: `document_id`, `table_id`, `field_id`

### Examples

```python
# Append paragraph
document_crud(method="append_text", document_id="...", table_id=17, field_id=29, text="Hello")

# Append bold text
document_crud(method="append_text", document_id="...", table_id=17, field_id=29, text="Important", bold=True)

# Append heading
document_crud(method="append_heading", document_id="...", table_id=17, field_id=29, text="Section", level=2)

# Append bullet list
document_crud(method="append_list", document_id="...", table_id=17, field_id=29, items=["Item 1", "Item 2"])

# Update block at position 2
document_crud(method="update_text", document_id="...", table_id=17, field_id=29, position=2, text="Updated content")

# Create new document
document_crud(method="create", table_id=17, field_id=29, title="My Document")

# Read to see structure
document_crud(method="read", document_id="...", table_id=17, field_id=29)
```

### Notes

- Always `list` first to get document IDs
- `position` is 0-based block index
- Use `read` to see current structure before updating
- `row_id` for create: omit to create new row, provide to add to existing
